Acknowledgements
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WinMac is an independent implementation. Its modules were written from scratch
against public macOS APIs, but their behaviour is modelled on — and inspired by —
the following open-source projects. No source code was copied from them.

  * Rectangle            https://github.com/rxhanson/Rectangle          (MIT)
      Window snapping: keyboard halves/thirds/quarters, drag-to-snap, size cycle.

  * AltTab               https://github.com/lwouis/alt-tab-macos        (GPL-3.0)
      Window switcher: per-window (not per-app) switching, MRU order, HUD actions.

  * SwiftQuit            https://github.com/onmyway133/SwiftQuit        (GPL-3.0)
      Auto-quit: terminate an app when its last window is closed.

  * LinearMouse          https://github.com/linearmouse/linearmouse     (MIT)
      Pointer control: separating acceleration from speed via IOHID service
      properties, and re-applying them when a device connects or the system wakes.
      The `Sources/MousePointer/` IOKit SPI shim adapts LinearMouse's PointerKit
      approach.

Because WinMac's window switcher and auto-quit behaviour are modelled on
GPL-3.0 projects, WinMac as a whole is distributed under the GPL-3.0.

The Windows-style names used in the UI ("Ctrl → Cmd", "⌥V pano geçmişi", the
blue snap overlay, etc.) describe Windows conventions and are not affiliated
with or endorsed by Microsoft.

BetterMouse (https://better-mouse.com) is a separate, closed-source commercial
application. No BetterMouse code is used in WinMac.
